# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search-tool exclusions. Read by ripgrep, fd, and the file-search layer of most
# agent tooling; NOT read by git. Anything here stays fully tracked, fully
# committed, and fully visible to `git status` — it is only kept out of
# project-wide text searches and fuzzy file pickers.
#
# This file exists for the cases where .gitignore is the wrong instrument:
# vendored trees that must stay in history, and submodules whose paths must
# keep reporting their state to git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# glm — a header-only math submodule, 1,670 files. Gitignoring a submodule path
# would suppress its status reporting, so it is excluded here instead. Nothing
# in Earthcall needs to grep glm's implementation; the API is documented
# upstream and the headers are included, never edited.
third_party/glm/

# The vendored dependency sources, restated here so the exclusion holds even for
# tools that read .ignore but not .gitignore.
local_deps/
third_party/asio/
third_party/flatbuffers/
third_party/glfw/
third_party/websocketpp/

# Generated / machine-local trees. Duplicated from .gitignore for the same
# reason: a tool that honours only one of these two files should still skip them.
build/
build2/
build_ag/
build_agy/
build-*/
build_logs/
cmake-build-*/
node_modules/
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Runtime save output — 2.0 GB, individual files up to 98 MB.
saves/games/

# Dear ImGui's bundled examples, per-backend demos and manual. The backends and
# core headers stay searchable — Earthcall compiles against imgui.h and the
# GLFW/Metal backends directly, and those are worth grepping. The example
# applications (152 files, one per platform permutation) and the FAQ are not:
# they are upstream reference material, they never appear in a build, and the
# FAQ's 48 KB of prose matches almost any imgui-related search term.
imgui/examples/
imgui/docs/
imgui/misc/

# Single-file vendored headers that are large enough to dominate any search hit
# list and are never edited by hand. miniaudio.h alone is 4.0 MB; json.hpp is
# 898 KB. Both are upstream drops.
src/Singularity/Audio/miniaudio.h
src/json.hpp
third_party/httplib/httplib.h
